# Google Ads API Configuration
# Follow these steps to set up Google Ads API integration:

# 1. Go to https://ads.google.com/nav/selectaccount
# 2. Select your Google Ads account
# 3. Go to Tools & Settings > Setup > API Center
# 4. Create a new application or use existing one
# 5. Get your Developer Token (must be approved by Google)
# 6. Set up OAuth2 credentials in Google Cloud Console
# 7. Generate refresh token using OAuth2 flow

# Your Google Ads Customer ID (without dashes)
# Found in Google Ads account (upper right corner)
GOOGLE_ADS_CUSTOMER_ID=1234567890

# OAuth2 Client ID from Google Cloud Console
# Create OAuth2 credentials in Google Cloud Console API & Services
GOOGLE_ADS_CLIENT_ID=your-client-id.googleusercontent.com

# OAuth2 Client Secret from Google Cloud Console
GOOGLE_ADS_CLIENT_SECRET=your-client-secret

# OAuth2 Refresh Token (generated after user consent)
# Use Google Ads API OAuth2 flow to get this token
GOOGLE_ADS_REFRESH_TOKEN=your-refresh-token

# Developer Token from Google Ads API Center
# Must be approved by Google for production use
GOOGLE_ADS_DEVELOPER_TOKEN=your-developer-token

# Sync token for scheduled sync operations (secure random string)
# Used to authenticate scheduled sync requests
GOOGLE_ADS_SYNC_TOKEN=secure_random_sync_token_123

# Instructions for getting OAuth2 tokens:
# 1. Use Google OAuth2 Playground: https://developers.google.com/oauthplayground/
# 2. In "Step 1", select "Google Ads API v14" scope: https://www.googleapis.com/auth/adwords
# 3. Click "Authorize APIs" and sign in with your Google account
# 4. In "Step 2", click "Exchange authorization code for tokens"
# 5. Copy the "Refresh token" value to GOOGLE_ADS_REFRESH_TOKEN above
# 6. The "Access token" expires, but refresh token is permanent

# Testing your configuration:
# 1. Add these variables to your main .env file
# 2. Restart your backend server
# 3. Go to /admin/google-ads in your frontend
# 4. Click "Test Connection" to verify setup
# 5. If successful, you can sync ads automatically

# Production Notes:
# - Developer Token must be approved by Google for production use
# - Test accounts have limited functionality
# - Keep all credentials secure and never commit them to version control